# Port patch, "Rapid fire" (1.1.6, the project owner: Leon and every other playable character fire twice as fast; the app
# menu's Controls, off by default; runtime/rapid_fire.cpp). The game times a shot two ways. Guns with a wait: the
# handguns and magnums (pl_handgun.cpp fire step 1: the recoil's motion frame PlShotFrameTbl - 2, the firing-speed
# tune-up's table), the Matilda and the Red9 (wep17.cpp: frame 3 to the burst's next round, frame 11 to the end), the
# machine guns (pl_machine.cpp: 3 frames a round) and the rifles' frame counters (pl_rifle.cpp m_Work4): the wait is
# halved, as the tune-up shortens it (re4_rapid_fire_shot_frame / _wait / _step / _count_down); the machine guns fire
# every other round in the frame its wait ends (re4_rapid_fire_now: 1 and 2 frames, 20 rounds a second). Guns whose
# next shot waits for a hand movement (the shotgun's pump, the bolt, the rocket launcher, the bow, the mine thrower):
# their routine runs with the fire state's motion at double speed (re4_rapid_fire_begin / _end, the gun object's fire
# motion too). The knife, the grenades and the empty hand: unchanged. Off: as the game.
